--
-- QA triage, one coherent set (our functions only):
--
-- P3 educator state (#3, #4)
--   * adm_educator_actions(educator) -> text[]: THE action matrix, read by the
--     admin UI (list_educators / get_educator_detail return it as `actions`)
--     and enforced by adm_set_educator_state for admin calls:
--       suspended account                 reactivate, delete
--       approved + active                 deactivate, suspend, delete
--       approved + inactive               activate, delete
--       rejected                          reconsider (-> under_review), delete
--       changes_requested                 approve, reject
--       draft / pending / under_review    approve, request_changes, reject (+ start_review)
--       deleted                           nothing
--   * adm_educator_action_for(educator, target state) -> the action a write means.
--   * adm_set_educator_state: an admin write outside the matrix is refused
--     (22023, "… isn't available while the educator is …"). System and
--     self writes (registration, resubmission) are not matrix-checked.
--     A reject deactivates the account; leaving "rejected" (reconsider or the
--     educator's resubmission) reactivates it.
--   * Effective state: "rejected" now wins over an inactive account (so a
--     rejected educator still sees the reason and can resubmit); suspended /
--     deleted still win over everything. Same rule in list_educators and
--     get_educator_stats (their inline copies of the rule) and in the
--     list's "suspended" filter.
--   * adm_backfill_rejected_inactive(): idempotent; a rejected educator whose
--     account is still active becomes inactive. Run once below.
--   (#4 itself was a frontend bug: "Activate" called the in-memory mock store,
--   never the RPC. Fixed in EducatorProfile.jsx / EducatorVerification.jsx.)
--
-- P7 admin student detail (#14)
--   get_student_detail: enrolled_series = only this student's ACTIVE rows of
--   admin_series_enrollments (revoked ones were included), with real
--   tests_total / tests_done / progress / best_score / attempts (progress was
--   always 0). (The made-up series names were a frontend bug: fixed in
--   UserManagement.jsx / studentsApi.js.)
--
-- P4 item 5 tracker (#6)
--   adm_series_tracker_rows_ext(): adm_series_tracker_rows() plus origin,
--   creator_id, creator_name; an educator's own series with no assignments
--   reads "Independent" (not "No Assignments Yet"). list_series_tracker and
--   get_series_tracker_detail use it; the educator filter also matches the
--   creator of an independent series. Assignment counts are unchanged (the
--   creator is never counted as assigned).
--
-- Replaced (each edit marked "-- 20261104090000", the rest verbatim from the
-- file named above it): adm_educator_effective_state, adm_set_educator_state,
-- list_educators, get_educator_stats, get_educator_detail, get_student_detail,
-- list_series_tracker, get_series_tracker_detail.
